      <guid>https://0x4ngk4n.github.io/posts/first/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;del&gt;A little&lt;/del&gt; About me…&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I am Angkan and as of today, I have been in IT for about 14 years now.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Back when I started, I was doing tech support for firewalls which, while I didn’t enjoy much but got me hooked into how computers communicate. Fast forward few job hoops where I acquired skills such as scripting and nix fundamentals, I landed a role where I gained exposure to first hand cyber-attacks employed by attackers-in-the-wild. This was 10 years back from today. Attacks were mostly around lack of input validation, source to sink based, deterministic in nature and like many before me and after, I was also like &lt;strong&gt;wow ^~^&lt;/strong&gt; would be cool to be a hacker-at-work.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
